{
  "date": "2026-11-21",
  "category": "fintech",
  "title_zh": "微信支付改规则：很久没交易的商户可以自己解除限制",
  "title_en": "WeChat Pay changes its rules: merchants with no transactions for a long time can lift restrictions themselves",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "zh": "据移动支付网11月20日报道，微信支付的运营公司财付通发布公告说，从12月21日开始，如果机构商户因为长时间没有交易而被限制，解除限制的方法会改变。机构商户一般是通过服务商等合作伙伴接入微信支付的商户。",
      "en": "According to a November 20 report by Mpaypass, Tenpay, the company that runs WeChat Pay, issued an announcement saying that starting December 21, the way restrictions are lifted will change for institutional merchants that were restricted because they had no transactions for a long time. Institutional merchants are usually merchants that connect to WeChat Pay through partners such as service providers."
    },
    {
      "zh": "以前，这些商户要提交资料，进行申诉，才能解除限制。以后，商户只需要确认自己还想继续使用。",
      "en": "Before, these merchants had to submit documents and file an appeal before the restriction could be lifted. From now on, a merchant only needs to confirm that it still wants to keep using the service."
    },
    {
      "zh": "被限制的商户会收到通知，然后可以在“微信支付商家助手”小程序里自己完成确认，解除限制。",
      "en": "Restricted merchants will receive a notice, and can then complete the confirmation themselves in the \"WeChat Pay Merchant Assistant\" mini-program to lift the restriction."
    },
    {
      "zh": "服务商和渠道商以后不用再替商户申诉了。它们可以用“合作伙伴订阅”和“限制状态查询”这两个功能，看商户有没有被限制、有没有解除，再提醒商户自己处理。对于新出现的这种限制，微信支付也不再通过原来的两个接口发通知和提供查询。",
      "en": "Service providers and channel partners will no longer need to file appeals for merchants. They can use two features, \"partner subscription\" and \"restriction status query\", to see whether a merchant has been restricted or has had the restriction lifted, and then remind the merchant to handle it themselves. For new restrictions of this kind, WeChat Pay will also stop sending notices and providing queries through two of its original interfaces."
    }
  ],
